    "body": "Followup to https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41979\r\n\r\nProblem:\r\n`u_undo_and_forget()` and `u_forget_unchanged()` do similar undo-tree surgery: unlink a header, promote the alt branch it displaced.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nExtract common logic to `u_forget_header()`.\r\n\r\nBonus:\r\n- The `:undo!` copy now fixes `b_u_oldhead`, so after forgetting a root header, its alt branch is still listed by `undotree()`.\r\n- Freeing can no longer unlink the promoted branch: `uh_alt_prev` is cleared first. The old code relied on the forgotten header being the first sibling.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-18T14:51:35Z",
